<!--
	What the assistant Albert can do for each role of the application: the policy of the
	AiToolAccessService.

	As long as the policy below is commented out, every account that can log in can talk to Albert,
	and Albert can only read (the default baseline: tool groups model.read and data.read). What
	Albert reads is limited by the model-based security of the application (<security-config>):
	Albert acts as the logged-in account.

	To set the policy:

	1. Replace the role names "MyReader" and "MyWriter" by the roles of the application. A role must
	   be a role on the security root SecurityStructure#ROOT. A role that does not exist stops the
	   start.
	2. Remove the comment marks around <config>.
	3. Start the application and log in with an account of each role that is no administrator. An
	   administrator bypasses the policy.

	What the template sets:

	- <tool-access>: the tool groups of each role. MyReader reads, MyWriter also changes data. Albert
	  asks the account to approve each change. A <deny> wins over every grant.
	- <baseline/>: no tool group for accounts without one of these roles.
	- <background-allowlist>: the limit of a run without a person (scheduler, MCP). Mandatory as soon
	  as a role is named.
	- <agent-access default="none">: only these roles can talk to Albert (TL_SingleAgent).

	The policy is read at the start of the application. In the classic UI, an administrator can also
	edit it in "Administration > Access rights > Agent security", which writes this file.

	See the developer articles ai/adding-albert (step 5) and ai/security/tool-access-configuration.
-->
<application config:interface="com.top_logic.basic.config.ApplicationConfig$Config"
	xmlns:config="http://www.top-logic.com/ns/config/6.0"
>
	<services>
		<!--
		<config service-class="com.top_logic.tl.ai.core.security.AiToolAccessService">
			<instance class="com.top_logic.tl.ai.core.security.AiToolAccessService">
				<tool-access>
					<role name="MyReader">
						<grants>
							<grant group="model.read"/>
							<grant group="data.read"/>
						</grants>
						<denies>
							<deny group="data.write"/>
							<deny group="script"/>
							<deny group="egress"/>
							<deny group="model.structure"/>
							<deny group="agent.authoring"/>
						</denies>
					</role>
					<role name="MyWriter">
						<grants>
							<grant group="model.read"/>
							<grant group="data.read"/>
